<article>
  <div class="container">
     </div>


  

    <div class="ms-chapter" style="background-image: url(assets/images/chapter.jpg)">
      <div class="container-fluid" >
        <div class="container">
          <div class="ms-row ms-row-full" id="partial_1">
            <div class="ms-col-content">
              
  
  <h2  id="heading-1">Introduction to the Community</h2>
  
    <p>Shared Values, Stakeholder Groups and Expertise</p>
  
  
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  

<div class="container">
<div class="ms-row ms-row-two ms-text" id="partial_2">
  <div class="ms-col-content">
    <p>Six stakeholder groups are involved in a vision of collaborative and fair Diamond Open Access: academic libraries, Diamond Open Access publishers, Open Access projects, initiatives and infrastructures, research funding, scientific associations, and Diamond Open Access journals. These six groups are based on the stakeholder mapping of the AuROA project (<a tabindex="0" data-trigger="click hover" class="ms-inline ms-inline-reference" data-toggle="popover" data-placement="top" title="Cited Source" data-content="<p>AuROA – Autor:innen und Rechtssicherheit für Open Access. (2022). Publizieren und Open Access in den Geisteswissenschaften: Erkenntnisse aus dem Projekt AuROA zu den Stakeholdern im Publikationsprozess.</p><a class='mdi mdi-earth' href='https://ualresearchonline.arts.ac.uk/id/eprint/21669/' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'></a>" data-html="true">2022<i></i></a>), which in turn emerged from surveys of authors, workshops, other events, and personal discussions. Stakeholders in the Open Access publication process in the humanities were identified and adapted by us with regard to organisational and funding issues of Diamond Open Access.<a tabindex="0" data-trigger="click hover" class="ms-inline ms-inline-reference" data-toggle="popover" data-placement="top" title="Cited Source" data-content="<p>Henkes, L. M., Wrzesinski, M., &amp; Holscher Blackman, K. (2025). Open Access gemeinsam gemacht: Kollaborative Ansätze des wissenschaftlichen Publizierens. <em>Zenodo</em>.</p><a class='mdi mdi-earth' href='https://doi.org/10.5281/ZENODO.14800427' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'></a>" data-html="true"><i></i></a></p>
  </div>
  <div class="ms-col-marginal">
    <aside class="ms-aside-hint"><p><strong>Researchers</strong> are not designated as a separate stakeholder group, as unlike the other groups, they do not operate in an organised manner and are usually not involved in funding issues.<br />
Although not separately represented, researchers are of central importance for Diamond Open Access. Their contribution in the sense of a scholar-led approach is included in other stakeholder groups such as journals and publishers, for example as authors, reviewers or members of scientific boards.</p></aside>
<aside class="ms-aside-keystatement"><p>Details about the stakeholders</p></aside>
<aside class="ms-aside-bookmark"><p><a href="#akteure">Chapter Stakeholders</a></p></aside>
  </div>
</div>

<figure class="ms-row ms-row-two ms-plugin ms-plugin-figure" id="partial_3">
  <div class="ms-col-content">
    <a href="#3Modal" type="button" data-toggle="modal" data-target="#3Modal">

<object data="assets/images/figures/Diamond_EN.svg" type="image/svg+xml" class="img-fluid"></object>

</a>


  </div>
  <div class="ms-col-marginal">
    
<aside class="ms-aside-caption">
  <p><strong>Stakeholder Groups of the Diamond Open Access Community</strong>
      
        <br>Six stakeholder groups and their individual contributions to fair and collaborative Diamond Open Access
      
  </p>
</aside>





<aside class="ms-aside-licence">
  <p>Alexander von Humboldt Institute for Internet and Society (HIIG) | CC BY 4.0</p>
</aside>


<div class="btn-toolbar" role="toolbar" aria-label="Download and share buttons">
